In Java (especially Java 8 Functional Interfaces), Predicate and Function are both used in Streams and Lambda expressions,
 but they serve different purposes.

1️⃣ Predicate

A Predicate is used to test a condition and it always returns boolean (true / false).

Package

java.util.function.Predicate

Method

boolean test(T t)
Example
Predicate<Integer> isEven = n -> n % 2 == 0;

System.out.println(isEven.test(10)); // true
System.out.println(isEven.test(7));  // false
Common Use Case

Mostly used with filter() in streams.

List<Integer> nums = List.of(1,2,3,4,5,6);

nums.stream()
    .filter(n -> n % 2 == 0)
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Output:

2
4
6

Here n -> n % 2 == 0 is a Predicate.

2️⃣ Function

A Function is used to transform one value into another value.

Package

java.util.function.Function

Method

R apply(T t)

T → Input type

R → Return type

Example
Function<Integer, Integer> square = n -> n * n;

System.out.println(square.apply(5));

Output:

25
Common Use Case

Mostly used with map() in streams.

List<Integer> nums = List.of(1,2,3,4);

nums.stream()
    .map(n -> n * n)
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Output:

1
4
9
16
🔑 Key Differences (Interview Table)
| Feature              | Predicate       | Function       |
| -------------------- | --------------- | -------------- |
| Purpose              | Check condition | Transform data |
| Return Type          | `boolean`       | Any type `R`   |
| Method               | `test()`        | `apply()`      |
| Common Stream Method | `filter()`      | `map()`        |
| Example              | `n -> n > 10`   | `n -> n * 2`   |

🔹 Simple Way to Remember

Predicate → Question (True/False)
Is number even?

Function → Transformation
Convert number to square

💡 Interview Tip (Very Common Question)

Example combining Predicate + Function

List<Integer> nums = List.of(1,2,3,4,5);

nums.stream()
    .filter(n -> n % 2 == 0)  // Predicate
    .map(n -> n * n)          // Function
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Flow:

1,2,3,4,5
 ↓ filter (even)
2,4
 ↓ map (square)
4,16

